# Online Event Registration System (HTML + CSS + JavaScript only)

## How to run it
No server needed — just open `index.html` in a browser (double-click it, or right-click →
Open with → your browser). Everything runs client-side.

Optional (recommended): serve it with a simple local server instead of `file://`, since some
browsers restrict `localStorage` on the `file://` protocol:
```bash
# from inside the project folder
python3 -m http.server 8000
# then visit http://localhost:8000/
```
Or in VS Code, install the "Live Server" extension and click "Go Live".

## Demo login
A default admin account is seeded automatically the first time the app loads:
- **Email:** admin@example.com
- **Password:** admin123

## Pages
| Page | File |
|---|---|
| Home | `index.html` |
| Register | `register.html` |
| Login | `login.html` |
| Event List | `events.html` |
| My Registrations | `my-registrations.html` |
| Admin Panel | `admin.html` |

## How each PHP/MySQL concept maps to this version
| Original (PHP + MySQL) | This version |
|---|---|
| MySQL `users`, `events`, `registrations` tables | JSON arrays in `localStorage`, managed in `js/db.js` |
| `$_SESSION` + idle timeout | `sessionStorage` session object (clears when the tab closes) with a 15-minute inactivity expiry, managed in `js/auth.js` |
| `password_hash()` / `password_verify()` | Plain string comparison (⚠️ not secure — demo only) |
| PDO prepared statements | Plain JS array methods (`find`, `filter`, `map`) |
| `includes/header.php` / `footer.php` | `js/nav.js` renders the nav bar into every page |
| Server-side redirect (`header("Location: ...")`) | `window.location.href = '...'` |

## Features included
- Registration, login, logout with **real session-based auth**:
  - Session lives in `sessionStorage`, so it automatically ends when the browser tab is closed (unlike the old version, which used `localStorage` and never expired).
  - 15-minute inactivity timeout — any click/keypress/scroll resets the clock; going idle past that logs the user out and redirects to `login.html?expired=1` with a "session expired" notice.
- Browse events, register, cancel registration, view "my registrations"
- Capacity limits enforced (can't over-register an event)
- **Admin panel** (`admin.html`, protected by `requireLogin()` + `requireAdmin()`):
  - Add / edit / delete events
  - View participants for a single event
  - **New:** an "All Registrations" tab showing every registration across every event in one table (event, participant, email, registered-on)
- Full CRUD on events and registrations, all client-side

### Session timeout details
`SESSION_TIMEOUT_MS` in `js/auth.js` controls the idle timeout (default 15 minutes). Note this is a per-tab session (a browser-standard `sessionStorage` limitation): opening the app in a second tab starts a separate session there, same as most vanilla sessionStorage-based demos.
